note<-c("# Method note: PreDraftWorkerPools1944, v2","","## Existing-code inventory","","| Table | Script | Output | Key definitions |","|---|---|---|---|","| 1 | Regressions/SummaryStats.R | SummaryStats.tex | position rank and nested hierarchy |","| 3 | MainResults/ByDistance/code/ByDistance_DraftKakari_Regressions.R | ByDistance_DraftKakari_Results.tex and coefficient CSV | cells, male drafts, arrivals |","| 6 | MainResults/BilateralTransferFlowPPML/code/BilateralTransferFlowPPML.R | bilateral-flow CSVs and RDS panels | office-level occupational cosine similarity |","| 9 | MainResults/Promotion/code/Promotion_Regressions.R | TransferOutcomes_Combined.tex | rank gain and promotion outcomes |","","## Definitions and sources","","I strip whitespace from position to form pos_norm, following Regressions/SummaryStats.R:17-22. I rename rank to court_rank and apply the employment-rank rule at Regressions/SummaryStats.R:30-42. I join normalized ka through ka_group_map.csv as at Regressions/NewTable1c_TransferType.R:38-47, and use normalized kyoku and kyoku groups from Regressions/NewTable1c_TransferType.R:55-125.","","I define cells and male draft counts as at MainResults/ByDistance/code/ByDistance_DraftKakari_Regressions.R:233-240, and reuse arrival classes from lines 177-191. Table 6 defines office-composition cosine similarity at MainResults/BilateralTransferFlowPPML/code/BilateralTransferFlowPPML.R:251-302, not pairwise occupation similarity, so I use exact pos_norm matches.","","## Diagnostics before results","",paste0("The mapping leaves ",sum(is.na(w44a$employment_rank))," of ",nrow(w44a)," workers unranked (",sprintf("%.2f",100*missrank),"%). I drop ",exc$unknown_title," Unknown, ",exc$concurrent_title," å…¼, and ",exc$rank_outside_1_3," ranks outside 1-3."),paste0("The 1942 directory covers ",paste(paste0(gov42$gov_level," (",gov42$workers," workers)"),collapse=", "),". tables/link_rate_by_kyoku.csv reports linkage."),paste0("The raw 1944 data have ",dup$raw_1944_rows," rows for ",dup$distinct_workers," workers: ",dup$exact_duplicate_excess," excess rows are exact duplicates and ",dup$nonexact_duplicate_excess," are alternative OCR/hierarchy/position assignments. I keep the first source-order row, matching the main tables."),"","## Sample and variables","",paste0("The panel has ",nrow(p)," male cells and ",nrow(w44)," eligible male workers. It contains ",sum(w44$drafted%in%TRUE)," drafted men; I export and exclude ",nrow(dw)," drafted women. Staff_ko excludes draftees. The incumbent union contains ",nrow(inc)," men."),paste0("Unknown distance is ",sprintf("%.2f",100*pd$lateral_unknown_share),"% of lateral pool membership, ",sprintf("%.2f",100*pd$promotion_unknown_share),"% of promotion pool membership, and ",sprintf("%.2f",100*ad$unknown_share),"% of arrivals."),"","## Table 3 consistency check","",paste0("The 1944 coefficients are Total internal = ",sprintf("%.4f",t3$estimate[t3$outcome=="total_internal"])," and New hires = ",sprintf("%.4f",t3$estimate[t3$outcome=="new_hires"]),"; published full-period values are ",sprintf("%.4f",t3$published_estimate[t3$outcome=="total_internal"])," and ",sprintf("%.4f",t3$published_estimate[t3$outcome=="new_hires"]),". Both signs match."),"","## Estimation and specifications","","I run OLS with kyoku and occupation fixed effects, kyoku- and ka-clustered inference, and restricted-null six-point Webb score-bootstrap p-values with 9,999 draws for every OLS interaction. I run PPML, Staff >= 3, ignore-track promotion, observed-ka, and high-link-kyoku robustness specifications. The CSVs retain warnings and specification_failures.csv records failures.",paste0("Recorded failures or warnings: ",nrow(fails),"."),"","## Changes from v1","","I use the full SummaryStats rank rule, exclude draftees from Staff, use the main-table cell and hierarchy definitions, classify missing-ka distances as unknown, add Webb inference and ka clustering, and run every requested robustness.","","## Five-line coefficient summary","",paste0(seq_along(five),". ",five));writeLines(note,file.path(out,"method_note.md"),useBytes=TRUE)
